On-target tests (Unity, replaces main.cpp with test/main.cpp):

```
RUN_TESTS=1 idf.py -B build-tests flash      # runs the full software unit suite by default
```

Read the Unity output with `etc/fugu_console.py -p /dev/cu.usbmodem...` (it resets the board on
connect, re-running the suite) — not `idf.py monitor`. The PWM/MCPWM tests are gated behind
`#if WITH_MCPWM` and only run in an MCPWM build (`CONFIG_FUGU_WITH_MCPWM=y`); the software suite
runs and passes without it.

Host-side tests (clang/g++, no flash needed):

```
clang++ -std=gnu++17 -fexceptions -I test/host-stub -I src \
    -o /tmp/service-test test/host-stub/service-test.cpp && /tmp/service-test
```

Each `test/host-stub/*-test.cpp` is self-contained; ESP-IDF headers are shimmed in
`test/host-stub/` (`esp_log.h`, `Arduino.h`, `freertos/{FreeRTOS,queue}.h`).
